SUBDEEP["patrick-stewart-dies-86"]=dict(intro=f"<b>Sir Patrick Stewart has died at 86.</b> The British actor, who carried Shakespearean training into two of the biggest franchises in film and television, died on Wednesday, October 28, at his home in Los Angeles, according to <a href=\"{_AP}\" {EXT}>the Associated Press</a>. His longtime spokesperson announced the news on Thursday, October 29. His family said he died in the loving care of his wife, the singer Sunny Ozell, the <a href=\"{_BBC}\" {EXT}>BBC</a> reported.",
facts=[("Died","Wed Oct 28, 2026, at home in Los Angeles"),("Age","86 (born July 13, 1940, Mirfield, Yorkshire)"),("Announced","Thu Oct 29, by his longtime spokesperson"),("Best known for","Capt. Jean-Luc Picard (Star Trek) and Prof. Charles Xavier (X-Men)"),("Stage","Royal Shakespeare Company from the 1960s; Waiting for Godot with Ian McKellen"),("Honours","Knighted for services to drama in 2010")],
body=f'''<h2>From Yorkshire to the Royal Shakespeare Company</h2><p>Stewart was born in Mirfield, West Yorkshire, in 1940 and grew up in a working-class household. He trained at the Bristol Old Vic Theatre School and joined the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1966, where he spent years in classical roles. For most of his first two decades as an actor he was a stage performer first, with television and film work on the side.</p>
<p>That background is why so many tributes focus on his voice and his discipline. The <a href="{_GU}" {EXT}>Guardian</a> called him a titan of stage and screen, renowned for both Shakespeare and sci-fi, which is a rare pairing.</p>
<h2>Captain Picard and a late, global fame</h2><p>In 1987, at 47, Stewart was cast as Captain Jean-Luc Picard in <i>Star Trek: The Next Generation</i>. The series ran for seven seasons, to 1994, and was followed by four feature films, from <i>Generations</i> (1994) to <i>Nemesis</i> (2002). He returned to the role two decades later in <i>Star Trek: Picard</i>, which ran for three seasons from 2020 to 2023. Picard's calm authority, shaped by his stage work, made the character one of the most quoted in science fiction.</p>
{_fig("ent-living-room-starfield","Plenty of fans are planning a rewatch this week. Illustration: AI-generated image.")}
<h2>Professor X</h2><p>A second franchise followed in 2000, when Stewart played Professor Charles Xavier in <i>X-Men</i>. He played the role across the original film series and in <i>Logan</i> (2017), widely seen as his farewell to it, then made a surprise return in <i>Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness</i> (2022). Marvel Studios was among those who posted tributes, <a href="https://apnews.com/article/patrick-stewart-dead-tributes-reactions-5d771fd5af52070e23cf081b31754393" {EXT}>AP reported</a>.</p>
<h2>Back on stage, and a friendship with Ian McKellen</h2><p>Stewart never left the theatre. He played Macbeth and Shylock, toured a one-man <i>A Christmas Carol</i>, and starred with Ian McKellen in <i>Waiting for Godot</i> in London and on Broadway. The two had played rivals Professor X and Magneto on screen and were close friends off it. McKellen led the tributes, calling Stewart "the most respected and beloved actor of his generation," <a href="{_BBC}" {EXT}>the BBC reported</a>. William Shatner and Hugh Jackman also paid tribute, <a href="https://apnews.com/article/patrick-stewart-dead-tributes-reactions-5d771fd5af52070e23cf081b31754393" {EXT}>per AP</a>.</p>
<h2>Beyond acting</h2><p>He was knighted in 2010 for services to drama. He also published a memoir, <i>Making It So</i>, in 2023.</p>
<h2>How to rewatch</h2><p>Streaming rights change by country. In the US, the Star Trek series are generally on Paramount+, and the X-Men films move between services. Check a guide such as JustWatch for your region before you pay for anything.</p>
<h2>Why it's trending</h2><p>Few actors are central to two franchises at once. The news broke on Thursday, Oct 29, and tributes have run all week, from theatre colleagues, co-stars and studios to fans sharing their favourite Picard scenes.</p>''',
faq=[("When did Patrick Stewart die?","On Wednesday, October 28, 2026, at his home in Los Angeles. The news was announced on October 29."),("How old was Patrick Stewart?","He was 86. He was born on July 13, 1940, in Mirfield, Yorkshire."),("Where did Patrick Stewart die?","At his home in Los Angeles, in the care of his wife, Sunny Ozell, his family said."),("What is Patrick Stewart best known for?","Playing Captain Jean-Luc Picard in Star Trek: The Next Generation and Star Trek: Picard, and Professor Charles Xavier in the X-Men films, alongside decades of Shakespeare on stage.")])
SUBDEEP["nascar-championship-homestead-2026"]=dict(intro=f"<b>The 2026 NASCAR Cup Series title comes down to three drivers.</b> After Sunday's race at Martinsville, only Kyle Larson, Christopher Bell and Denny Hamlin can still win the championship at Homestead-Miami Speedway on <b>Sunday, Nov 8, at 3 p.m. ET on NBC</b>, per <a href=\"{_WS}\" {EXT}>NASCAR</a>. Larson leads Bell by 67 points and Hamlin by 70, so he can clinch with as few as nine points, according to <a href=\"{_CR}\" {EXT}>NASCAR's Chase Report</a>.",
facts=[("Race","Cup Series championship race, Homestead-Miami Speedway"),("When","Sun Nov 8, 2026, 3 p.m. ET (noon PT)"),("TV","NBC; pre-race coverage from 2 p.m. ET"),("Still eligible","Kyle Larson, Christopher Bell, Denny Hamlin"),("Gap","Larson +67 on Bell, +70 on Hamlin"),("Larson's number","9 points, or 28th place with no stage points")],
body=f'''<h2>What happened at Martinsville</h2><p>William Byron dominated Sunday's race at Martinsville Speedway, winning both stages and the race for his first victory of 2026. But he had already been eliminated from the title fight, so the win did not change the championship picture, <a href="{_YH}" {EXT}>Yahoo Sports</a> reported.</p>
<p>The title contenders had quieter days. Larson lost a lap after an early strategy call and fought back to ninth. Hamlin finished sixth and Bell tenth, and neither scored stage points, so they barely cut into Larson's lead. Chase Briscoe (14th), Joey Logano (18th), Tyler Reddick (12th) and Ryan Blaney (35th, after contact with Josh Berry) all fell out of mathematical contention.</p>
<h2>The championship math</h2><p>This year's Chase is a points race: there's no four-driver, winner-takes-all final like in recent seasons. Whoever has the most points after Homestead is champion. With 13 of the 16 Chase drivers now out, the math is simple:</p>
<ul><li><b>Kyle Larson</b> clinches by scoring nine points, whatever Bell and Hamlin do. If he scores no stage points, finishing 28th or better is enough, per <a href="{_CR}" {EXT}>NASCAR</a>.</li><li><b>Christopher Bell</b> (-67) and <b>Denny Hamlin</b> (-70) both need a big day and real trouble for Larson. As Yahoo noted, even a win would not guarantee either of them the title.</li></ul>
{_fig("sports-stock-car-pit-stop","Pit road can decide a points race. Illustration: AI-generated image.")}
<h2>Who the contenders are</h2><p><b>Larson</b>, 34, drives the No. 5 Hendrick Motorsports Chevrolet and is going for his third Cup championship. <b>Bell</b>, 31, drives the No. 20 Joe Gibbs Racing Toyota, and <b>Hamlin</b>, 45, drives the No. 11 Joe Gibbs Racing Toyota; neither has won a Cup title. For Hamlin, one of the sport's most successful drivers without a championship, Sunday may be one of his last real shots. The full field is on <a href="{_EL}" {EXT}>NASCAR's Homestead entry list</a>.</p>
<h2>How to watch</h2><p>The race starts at <b>3 p.m. ET</b> (2 p.m. CT, noon PT, 8 p.m. in the UK) on <b>NBC</b>, with pre-race coverage from 2 p.m. ET. Times are from <a href="{_WS}" {EXT}>NASCAR's championship weekend schedule</a>. Homestead-Miami is a 1.5-mile oval south of Miami, and its worn surface usually rewards drivers who can run right against the wall.</p>
<h2>What to watch for</h2><ul><li><b>The early stages.</b> If Larson scores stage points in the first two stages, he could all but lock up the title before the final run.</li><li><b>Pit road.</b> A penalty or a slow stop is the likeliest way for a 67-point lead to shrink.</li><li><b>Spoilers.</b> Byron, Logano, Blaney and the rest of the eliminated drivers are still racing for a win, and any of them could take points away from the contenders.</li></ul>''',
faq=[("When is the NASCAR championship race in 2026?","Sunday, November 8, 2026, at 3 p.m. ET at Homestead-Miami Speedway in Florida."),("What channel is the NASCAR championship on?","NBC, with pre-race coverage starting at 2 p.m. ET."),("Who can win the 2026 NASCAR Cup title?","Only Kyle Larson, Christopher Bell and Denny Hamlin are still mathematically eligible."),("What does Kyle Larson need to clinch?","Nine points. If he scores no stage points, a 28th-place finish or better clinches it.")])
